    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1343">

                <pb facs="0903" n="787" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg787"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/106.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Ambassador Willard.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your January 6. Inform King contents Department’s January 5, and also that
                    Department has directed American Consul, Chihuahua, to investigate and report as
                    to killing of two Spanish subjects. You will be informed regarding report.</p>
                <p>Consul, Hermosillo, reports that Constitutionalist leaders have heard no
                    complaint of mistreatment Spaniards, Parral, but are investigating by
                    telegraph.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
